A||N||5||steves||Losing pressure in clutch line||||1||
Z||000000||steves||07-06-2000||07:42 PM||||Hi Folks, I've looked to see if I could ever help, but it looks like I'll need help first!<BR>I have an 87 GT 5spd with the pushrod 3.4. Problem is that with the clutch pedal fully down, the clutch will SOMETIMES start to engage (as when backing up and waiting for traffic to clear..quite fun) There is zero fluid loss, and no apparent leak at the slave.  Using what I thought was great logic, I replaced the clutch master... twice (the second time I checked for pressure loss with a gauge. There was consistantly zero pressure loss.) <BR>Ok...So I think I have a good master, non leaking slave, non leaking system, fully bled (several times). With the clutch pedal fully depressed, I have had a friend in the back of the car witness the slave piston slowly moving back to engage the clutch.  Once again, this happens only on occassion.<P>Any ideas?  Can the hose under the car expand just enough to cause a loss in pressure? Has anyone replaced this hose/tube/line?<BR>Thanks, Steve||||reg||1
Z||000001||Vader||07-07-2000||11:18 PM||||Steve,<P>Your clutch throwout fork (lever) could be doing this:<P> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.juno.com/jlstrey/files/clutchfork.jpg"> <P>Later,<BR>Vader<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"||||reg||1
Z||000002||350ZZ4||07-09-2000||06:29 AM||||Mine loses pressure too, and it gets far worse in hot weather. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||RobertVol||07-09-2000||01:49 PM||||I agree with Vader. Usually I heard called a throw out bearing but fork . But anyway sometimes you can tell..Engage the clutch and give it alot of gas. Usually on the fieros I have seen this happen  it will not onlt start to engage it will do it over and over . like grab and let go and then grab and then let go again. while hitting the gas. Kinda like a "thud ,thud ,thud' and you will feel it. <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR> [URL=http://drive.to/North Florida Fiero Club[/URL] <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/247a8740.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||350ZZ4||10-16-2000||06:28 PM||||In my 2m4 I have power but I turn the key with no response, not even a click. No power drain either.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||10-16-2000||06:49 PM||||350zz,<P>That sounds like a bent clutch pedal to me.  There is a multitude of information that has been covered on that topic in the past.  Perform a search and if you still have questions ask again or refer to Ed Park's Fiero Factory web page (not the British Fiero Factory).  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
